    intermediate type of file that is neither human-readable nor
    directly executable.  Subsequent steps, most importantly
    linking, take over from there and produce the final result.
    In practice, however, this distinction is mostly only important
    when you're developing the build process (or, heaven help you,
    writing a compiler).  If all you're doing is patching and
building,
    the entire build process is for all practical purposes one atomic
    step to you, and we commonly use the word "compiling" for it.


